Preliminary API Concepts for Single Entry Point (subject to change) - v 0.1

GET - USED TO RETRIEVE DATA FROM THE SERVER

#
GET /digital-twins/endpoints
Retrieve a list of registered external RDF endpoints available for federated querying.
#
GET /metadata/endpoints
List available metadata repositories (internal and external).#
GET /digital-twins/{id}/contributors
Retrieve a list of users or institutions that contributed to a specific Digital Twin.
#
GET /digital-twins/{id}/history
Retrieve the version history of a Digital Twin, including changes to metadata, structure, or linked media.
#
GET /digital-twins/{id}/usage
Show how often a Digital Twin has been accessed, used in tools, or cited.
#
GET /user-spaces/{id}/files

Retrieve a list of files uploaded by the user.

Potential Parameters:
userId: The ID of the user requesting the files.
fileType: Filter files by type (e.g. rdf, video, csv).
visibility: Filter files by visibility (e.g., private, public).
tags: Filter files by tags (e.g., Cyprus, 2025).
createdAfter: Retrieve files created after a specific date.
sortBy: Sort files by a specific attribute (e.g., uploadDate).
order: Order of sorting (e.g., asc, desc).
#
GET /digital-twins

Retrieve a list of Digital Twins based on a federated query across local and external RDF sources. 
This allows users to discover Digital Twins not only stored in ECHOES but also in registered external endpoints.

Potential Parameters:

userId: The ID of the user requesting the Digital Twins.
query: A SPARQL query used to retrieve Digital Twins across sources.
sources: List of RDF sources to query (e.g., echoes, externalEndpoint1, externalEndpoint2).
includeMetadata: Include metadata in the response.
includeLinkedMedia: Include linked media in the response. 
hasMedia: Filter Digital Twins that have associated media.

##########################################################################################################################################
POST - USED TO SEND NEW DATA TO THE SERVER

POST /digital-twins/endpoints/register
Register an external SPARQL endpoint for federated querying.

Potential Parameters:
userId: The ID of the user registering the endpoint.
endpointUrl: URL of the external SPARQL endpoint.
accessPolicy: Access policy for the endpoint (e.g., read-only, read-write).
contactEmail: Contact email for the endpoint.
supportedOntologies: List of supported ontologies for the endpoint.
#
POST - USED TO SEND NEW DATA TO THE SERVER

POST /digital-twins/create

Create a new Digital Twin using metadata from a local source or a federated endpoint. 
The metadata is processed using a selected Virtual Application (VA), and the resulting 
Digital Twin is stored either in ECHOES or in a registered external endpoint.

Potential Parameters:
userId: The ID of the user creating the Digital Twin
metadataSource: Defines the source of metadata (e.g. local vs federated, SPARQL query to retrieve metadata)
vaToolId: ID of the Virtual Application used to process the metadata
storageTarget: Where to store the Digital Twin (local vs federated)
visibility: Visibility of the Digital Twin (e.g., private, public).
#
POST /digital-twins/preview

Process metadata using a selected Virtual Application (VA) to preview the resulting Digital Twin structure, 
without saving it. Metadata can come from a local source or a federated endpoint.

Potential Parameters:

userId: The ID of the user requesting the preview.
metadataSource: Defines the source of metadata.
vaToolId: ID of the Virtual Application used to process the metadata.
outputFormat: Desired format of the preview (e.g., JSON, RDF, TTL).
#
POST /digital-twins/{id}/enrich

Enrich an existing Digital Twin with new data (RDF triples), metadata or media.

Potential Parameters:
userId: The ID of the user enriching the Digital Twin.
twinId: ID of the Digital Twin to be enriched.
data: Data to be added to the Digital Twin.
media: Media files to be added to the Digital Twin.
metadata: Metadata associated with the new data or media.
visibility: Visibility of the new data or media (e.g., private, public).
#
PUT /digital-twins/{id}/update

Update the content of an existing Digital Twin, including its RDF data, metadata, or linked media. 
This endpoint replaces or modifies existing elements rather than adding new ones.

Potential Parameters:

userId: The ID of the user performing the update.
twinId: ID of the Digital Twin to be updated.
updatedData: RDF data to replace or modify existing content.
updatedMetadata: Updated metadata fields (e.g., title, description, tags).
updatedMedia: Updated or replaced media files.
visibility: Updated visibility settings (e.g., private, public).
changeNote: Optional description of the update for version tracking.
#
PUT /digital-twins/{id}/permissions

Update access permissions for a Digital Twin.

Potential Parameters:
userId: The ID of the user updating the permissions.
twinId: ID of the Digital Twin.
permissions: New permissions for the Digital Twin.
#
POST /user-spaces/{id}/share

Share a file or Digital Twin with another user or group of users.

Potential Parameters:

userId: The ID of the user sharing the resource.
resourceId: The ID of the resource to be shared (e.g., file or Digital Twin).
targetUserId: The ID of the user or group the resource is being shared with.
permissions: Access level granted (e.g., read-only, read-write).
expirationDate: Optional expiration date for the shared access.
notify: Whether to notify the recipient (true/false).
message: Optional message to include with the share action.
